CRITERIA	                  BOOTSTRAP     	                    TAILWIND CSS	                         REACT COMPONENT LIBRARY
Development Speed	          Fast (pre-built components)	        Moderate (utility-first, more manual)	 Very fast (ready-made React components)
Customization Flexibility	  Limited (theme overrides needed)    High (fully customizable)	             Moderate (can be customized with effort)
Design Consistency	        High (standardized components)	    Depends on team discipline	           High (consistent design system)
Long-term Maintenance	      Good (stable, but legacy concerns)	Excellent (growing adoption)	         Good (well-maintained, but major version upgrades can be disruptive)
React Ecosystem Integration	Requires React-Bootstrap	          Seamless (works with any React setup)	 Excellent (built for React)
Bundle Size & Performance	  Larger (full CSS bundle)	          Optimizable (PurgeCSS removes unused styles)	Moderate (tree-shaking helps)

Recommendation: Material-UI (MUI) / Ant Design because it has:
faster development with pre-built React components (tables, charts, forms).
better React integration (no additional adapters needed).
design consistency enforced by the library.
good balance between customization and speed.

Implementation Strategy & Timeline
Week 1-2: Setup & Prototyping
Install MUI/Ant Design + dependencies.
Build a basic layout (sidebar, navigation, data grid).
Define a theme (colors, typography).

Week 3-5: Core Dashboard Development
Implement sales analytics (charts using Recharts or Chart.js).
Build inventory management tables (MUI DataGrid or Ant Design Table).
Staff scheduling (drag-and-drop calendar with React Big Calendar).

Week 6: Testing & Optimization
Performance checks (bundle size, lazy loading).
Cross-browser/device testing.
Final UI polish.

Week 7: Deployment & Documentation
Deploy using Vercel/Netlify.
Document design system usage for future scaling.
Total Estimated Time: 6-7 weeks (adjust based on team size).

DESIGN SYSTEM STRATEGY
Component Reusability Standards
Atomic Design Implementation:
Create a structured hierarchy of components:
Atoms: Basic UI elements (buttons, inputs, icons)
Molecules: Simple combinations (search bar = input + button)
Organisms: Complex components (data cards, filter panels)
Templates: Page layouts
Pages: Final compositions

mplementation Rules:

1.Props API Standardization:
// All interactive components follow this pattern
<Button
  variant="primary|secondary|text"
  size="sm|md|lg"
  disabled={boolean}
  onClick={handler}
  aria-label={string}
/>

2.Compound Components for complex patterns:
<DataTable>
  <DataTable.Header>
    <DataTable.Column accessor="name" />
  </DataTable.Header>
  <DataTable.Body data={data} />
  <DataTable.Pagination />
</DataTable>

3.Styled System Props for consistent styling:
<Box
  p={3}          // padding
  bg="neutral.100" // background
  borderRadius="md"
/>
